            "id": "levelled_description_0101b4838f77",
            "level": {
              "value": 4
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "You know staying cool is key to prevailing in social situations, as anger leads to mistakes. When a creature you're interacting with decreases its attitude from indifferent to unfriendly or from unfriendly to hostile, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to any attempts to Make an Impression on the creature for the next hour. If this decrease in attitude leads to combat, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the subsequent initiative roll instead."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
